{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917261300},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to:\n1. Find the total farmers markets from the first dataset (harvestlymarkets.com CSV)\n2. Get census data from the second dataset (census file with state population data)\n3. Calculate the ratio of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S., to four decimal places\n4. Provide one confident sentence\n5. Not mention unverified facts and use tools for math\n\nFirst, I should follow the xorq analyst procedure:\n1. Orient: Check if there are semantic models or existing aliases in the catalog\n2. Then ingest the datasets if needed\n3. Compute the value using xorq_select\n4. Verify with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog to see what's available.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's available in the catalog, then ingest these datasets and compute the answer."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01C2y8voUZNSPnywF4FYJ2Es","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01B5y9rLNjszBRqqJyRYyjPK","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":333,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8310,"totalTokens":8653,"cost":{"input":0.000